# SYNTHETIC / DERIVED fixture. Not a captured sweep.
# Built for the query tests that need 'the same endpoint sampled in two
# runs with different values', which no single real sweep can provide (one
# run cannot test most-recent-run logic).
#
# Construction: the full real run from run-with-samples.nq (run
# 2026-08-22T16:00:00Z, the CURRENT/most-recent sweep) is followed by a second
# copy of that same file with every occurrence of 2026-08-22T16:00:00Z
# rewritten to 2026-08-22T14:00:00Z (an earlier, STALE sweep of the same
# three endpoints, including kadaster, the endpoint these tests target).
# In the stale copy only, kadaster's single owl:Restriction sampledValue is
# swapped for <urn:sparqlwatch:test:stale-only-class>, a class that does not
# appear anywhere else in this file.
#
# CURRENT_ONLY_CLASS = <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Restriction>: present in the
#   current (16:00) run's kadaster sample, absent from the stale (14:00) one.
# STALE_ONLY_CLASS   = <urn:sparqlwatch:test:stale-only-class>: present only in
#   the stale (14:00) run's kadaster sample.
# A query answering what is in this endpoint for kadaster must return the
# 16:00 run's classes (CURRENT_ONLY_CLASS present) and never the 14:00 run's
# (STALE_ONLY_CLASS absent), because 14:00 is not the most recent run.
#
# One further hand edit on top of the mechanical rewrite, for the
# measurements query's most-recent-run test: kadaster's sw:metric:classes
# dqv:value in the STALE (14:00) run was changed from "verified" (the value
# the mechanical copy would have produced, matching the current run) to
# "indeterminate". Every other verdict is identical between the two runs
# because the mechanical copy changes nothing but the run IRI, so a
# most-recent-run test needs at least one verdict that actually differs. The
# CURRENT (16:00) run's kadaster classes verdict is unchanged: "verified".
# A query answering kadaster's verdicts must return "verified" for
# sw:metric:classes (the 16:00 run's value) and never "indeterminate" (the
# 14:00 run's), because 14:00 is not the most recent run.
